Overview of the certification process in NL:


First, *Manufacturer Certification* by the Netherlands Vehicle Authority (RDW):

# Okai to contact RDW by email and request an interview (no defined response timeline);
# After the interview, Okai has to fill in the application form {color:#ff5630}(estimated to be no more than three months);{color}
# RDW may or may not request a factory visit. Okai already has ISO9001 Quality certification, so this step is unlikely to happen.
# After a positive evaluation based on the application, Okai receives the CoP (Conformity of Production) and can start the type approval process {color:#ff5630}(estimated to be no more than twelve months);{color}

Second, *Certification of Product (Type Approval)* by the Netherlands Central Government:

# NL Central Government audit the manufacturer certification, and if the CoP is approved, Okai can request the Certification of Product (Type Approval), basically asking for approval from the Ministry of Infrastructure and Water Management;
# Central Government contacts RDW for an admission interview;
# RDW inspects the product to check if all the requirements are met, and reports the results back to the Central Government, which will approve it.
{color:#ff5630}(no estimated timelines for the Tye Approval){color}

