More information on Vodafone operator problems:

{{The root cause of this problem is that Vodafone profile does not support the same APN to activate PDP twice. Based on log analysis, the process is as follows: }}

{{1. The Vodafone profile is successfully downloaded and installed in Usim, and then Usim notifies the module to read the card again }}

{{2. Successfully re read the card, the module uses the APN (Terminal. apn, iptype: IPV4) configured by cgdcont and successfully registers with LTE to obtain the IP address }}

{{3. Usim requires the module open chanel to carry APN (Terminal. apn). At this time, Usim should want to send a notification of successful installation of Vodafone profile to the server through bip, }}

{{4. The default iptype for module bip is IPV4V6. Since the registered iptype is ipv4, the module does not reuse the registered IP address and initiate PDP activation to the network, }}

{{5. Vodafone rejected the activation request for this PDP, resulting in a failed notification sending }}

{{6. usim internal logic rolled back profile}}

