* Type: the bicycle must be suitable for urban use, comfortable, ergonomic and of the appropriate size for young people, adults, women or men;
* Design: The design of the bicycle must be clearly distinguishable from commercial and original bicycles, allowing easier identification of bicycles;
* Materials: the frame must be resistant to intensive use and climatic conditions;
* Lighting system: the bicycle must have at least one front and one rear light, which must be switched on automatically at the start of the rental period and switched off at the end of the rental period, again automatically, remaining on during use;
* Reflectors: reflectors must be placed at least on the pedals and rear mudguard;
* Horn: The horn must be installed on the handlebar;
* Pedals: pedals must have a non-slip function;
* Mudguards: the bicycle must have front and rear mudguards;
* Stand: The bicycle must have a stand that is easy to activate and can support the weight of the bicycle;
* Saddle: the saddle must be easily adjustable, with a locking system to avoid the extraction;
* Transmission: The bicycle transmission must be covered if a system requiring constant lubrication is used (e.g. chain drive);
* Cables and bicycle components: Cables and components should be incorporated into the bicycle frame as far as possible to minimise vandalism;
* Hubs and nuts: Hubs and nuts must be able to be opened with keys exclusive to the system in order to prevent theft of individual parts;
* Basket: the Basket must be easy to clean and must not allow the accumulation of waste and must ensure the stability of the parked vehicle;
* Electronic locking system: The bicycle locking/unlocking system must be remotely activated via a smartphone app and designed in such a way that the bicycle can be parked without being tied to a stand (rack).
* The battery should power front and rear lights during the whole ride
* The presence of a display indicating real time speed (in km/h) and battery SOC
