IMHO the BE should not be involved in the details of AIoT shutdown process. When BE sends {{AI_POWER_OFF}} then I propose this flow:

#  IoT receives {{AI_POWER_OFF}}
# IoT sends {{AI_SHUTDOWN}} to AIoT and waits for confirmation (should arrive immediately if no packet corruption on UART)
# IoT waits 4 seconds to allow AIoT to complete shutdown
# IoT cuts power to AIoT
# IoT acknowledges {{AI_POWER_OFF}}

